{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head `366618b60a931872fcddaba5a763b43224409e20`, on main `0459d7f5`. Main has since moved to `3e055104`, which adds only J5's note, so it shares no path with this head.\n\n**My three items from `aeaf2ab2`.**\n\n- **The reason line.** I read `reasonsOf` and `questionReasons`. Each reads the page from the query, and each takes the acts that the card actually offers, after `check-original` replaces them. So an item page never says \"Open this card\", and a merged change or a viewer with no grants reads \"Open this card to read the change.\" The IDs that `reasonsOf` tests are the IDs that `verdict` and `merging` build. `s4` holds an item page and a change with no acts, and both controls fail by assertion.\n- **The superseded read.** The new check runs after the port returns and before the second `#admit`, so it replaces the false words only where a signature can already exist. A refusal before the signature still comes from `#admit` inside the port's callback, with its own words. The control fails the named test. No run has hit this window, as the note says.\n- **The digest.** It now sits in the body's `Rules:` block.\n\n**Evidence.** `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-card-press-head-2/` verifies against `SHA256SUMS` `09c166a0…` and holds no writable file. The gate exits 0 at `a1f81b61`. Run 41345198903 of the card workflow succeeded at that commit, and the commits after it change only the note and its manifest, so the citation rule in `0998f9ec` holds for the card's bytes. The note says that its Chromium row and first-round controls ran at the earlier code, and this round changes no file under `packages/mcp/browser`.\n\nAt this head I ran `s4.test.mjs` (18 passed), `view-sessions.test.ts` (14 passed) and the seal test (10 passed). `check-notes` and `check-commit-messages` pass against `0459d7f5`, `check-doc-links` finds 0 broken links, and the worktree stays clean.\n\n**The timing table.** I recomputed the owner's rows from the app's log and the journal, and they match: calls 9, 17 and 18. Entries 72 and 74 are 64 minutes apart, so case D's gap is real.\n\n**Next edit, not blocking.** \"One run rules out the gap\" claims more than one run can. The run did not reproduce the extra time after a gap. The note's next sentences say that the cause stays undetermined and the machine's load is unknown, so a reader is not misled about the conclusion. \"One run did not reproduce it after the same gap\" would say what the run shows.\n\n**No app has run this.** The planner's `7429dad3` asks for one short session after this head lands, and that session is what can show the wait and the recovery in the app.\n\n**Architecture.** A timeout is a state that the card recovers from. The server's order decides what a stale press means, and I traced that in `aeaf2ab2`. Words now come from what the page offers. The head adds no server state beyond one wait constant.\n\n**Security.** No authority changes. The `service.ts` seal moves for one `export`. The card no longer says that nothing was sent after a read signed, on this path or on the no-answer path.\n\n**Simplification.** `reasonsOf` and `questionReasons` share a shape and differ in their nouns and act tests. Two copies are fine at this size, and the next edit that needs a third can join them.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e5025822240578e0cb4a1973e978c5bd95b1d949","binding":"assigned","head":"366618b60a931872fcddaba5a763b43224409e20","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d55d5fab98a4703daaa62ce7e61087fcbf1e2f8c\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3c7517361fc78a13f67e3f4d0e2c7b5c38a19746\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8268feb1f346003803e5146499c73a5eae65ccd5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}